---
code: mark-unknown-verb
when-fires: the new-grammar mark parser hit a period-free head/continuation token that is not a known verb (`281` §4 rule-3 miss). oracle/predict/parser.rs parse_mark.
why: 281 §4 keystone (rul-verbs-dotless-kinds-dotted): a dotless mark token is a verb; an unknown one is malformed committed syntax ⇒ the block drops to ⊤ (`inv-top-reject`). `{token}` = the bad token, `{expected}` = the known-verb vocabulary.
---
-- oracle.sh --
# dorc-lang/v0.2
foo__predict() { foo : frobnicate sm.dorc.X; }

